record.content:
{\bf Stokes' theorem}:\, The surface integral of the curl of a vector function is equal to the line integral of that vector function taken around the closed curve bounding that surface.

\begin{equation}
\int \int_S \nabla \times {\bf W} \cdot d {\bf a} = \oint_O {\bf W} \cdot d {\bf r} 
\end{equation}

On account of its great importance in all branches of mathematical physics a number of different proofs will be given.

\subsection{Proof I.}

